## The three closures I was told to distrust

**1. The Mongolian read-shape VETO — FALSIFIED on my own corpus.** The V78 closure kept the two arms it called "clause-level by construction". `MN_READ_PREDICATE` is not one of them: `байгаа` is Mongolian's ordinary attributive participle (`хүлээгдэж байгаа` = pending, `хоцорч байгаа` = lagging, `идэвхгүй байгаа` = inactive), so an imperative clause routinely *contains* a read predicate without being a read.

| build | ordinary mixed-turn requests swallowed | genuine reads correctly vetoed |
|---|---|---|
| candidate `6c1bfca9` | **11 of 20** | 5/5 |
| previous candidate `924977e4` | 7 of 20 | 3/5 |
| with my prepared fix | **3 of 20** (all three pre-existing) | 5/5 |

`Alpha-г битгий устга. Хүлээгдэж байгаа зөвшөөрлийг цуцла.` ("Don't delete Alpha. Cancel the pending approval.") → every model mutation field stripped at `:4369-4380`, and the receipt at `:8529` tells the founder *"you asked me not to, so nothing was executed."* That is **a mixed turn whose un-negated imperative is refused** — an explicit FAIL condition. The session's "0 of 4" was measured on `d2_veto_cost.mjs`, whose every row exercises the interrogative-**word** arm and none the predicate arm.

**2. The `MN_READ_SHAPE` byte-identity claim — TRUE.** Recomposed source is byte-identical (252 chars) and flags identical (`iu`) to the literal lifted out of `git show 924977e4:…`, 0 behavioural differences over 100 probes. The request tier did not change. Now pinned so a future split cannot change it silently.

**3. `NON_EXISTENCE_CLAIM` — FALSIFIED in the false-POSITIVE direction.** 0 false negatives on #78's own corpus (good), but **16 of 21** truthful sentences match, and executing the **real** denial-contradicted window, **3 of 5** truthful answers are replaced by "I could not confirm that from this turn" — `Alpha's end date is missing from the record.` (a null column), `The invoice for ACME was never created.`, `I found no record of overtime for Bat in September.` The two survivors survive **by accident**: `typeNamedIn` happened to extract the word `record` out of "there **is no** record". That is **a truthful READ rewritten on text shape alone** — the second explicit FAIL condition. The round's FP control set was three sentences, all of them assertions of *presence*.

